plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:167:## 9. Monorepo and AI-agent workflow
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:204:## 10. CI and build/release pipeline
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:208:Use Playwright browser tests for rapid UI behavior, plus packaged-app automation for IPC, real menus, focus, window creation, tool origin isolation, and PTY resizing. Browser WebKit tests do not establish WKWebView parity. Current Tauri documentation describes WebdriverIO's embedded server path on macOS/Windows; direct tauri-driver is limited to Windows/Linux. Keep embedded automation plugins debug/test-only and verify their absence from releases. Native capture permission tests still require an interactive signed session. [verified: https://v2.tauri.app/develop/tests/webdriver/] **[assumption: test strategy]**
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:216:3. On Mac, sign nested helpers and app with stable bundle identifiers and correct entitlements, enable hardened runtime, notarize, staple, and validate the downloaded DMG/app on a clean account. Test permission persistence across the N-1 update. Tauri documents Developer ID notarization and available credential methods. [verified: https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/sign/macos/]
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:217:4. On Windows, build on Windows, sign executables and installer through a managed signing identity, timestamp, verify signatures, and test clean install/uninstall/update including WebView2 provisioning. A valid signature is not a promise that reputation warnings never occur. [verified: https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/sign/windows/] **[assumption: validation policy]**
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:221:## 11. Product-killing risks and first proof
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:225:**Distribution:** ship direct-download notarized macOS builds, not a Mac App Store dependency. Apple's review guidelines restrict downloaded/executed code that changes functionality; the exact treatment of this product requires review, but a generated-tool architecture should not depend on a favorable store interpretation. Notarization is neither sandbox enforcement nor privacy certification. [verified: https://developer.apple.com/app-store/review/guidelines/] **[assumption: distribution choice]**
plan/research/11-architecture-codex.md:227:**Meta dependency/cost:** successful API-key auth for serve, provider terms for captured third-party data, Muse redistribution, and Windows binary/sandbox support remain explicit gates. Do not route screen data to an unverified endpoint or build a business model on unverified prices/context sizes. Enforce queue concurrency and admission budgets locally, while admitting that a running provider turn may overshoot a locally estimated budget. **[assumption]** [local: plan/BRIEF.md]
